        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-q" type="button" aria-expanded="false">How much does drone photography cost in Huddersfield?<span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">Cost depends on the size of the property, how many images you need and how far the site is from Huddersfield. A standard residential drone photography shoot for an estate agent listing is priced differently to a full commercial site survey. Send us the property address and a short brief and we will come back with a fixed, no-obligation quote.</div></div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-q" type="button" aria-expanded="false">Do I need permission to have my property photographed by drone?<span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">You do not need permission to photograph your own property, but we do need permission from whoever controls the land we take off and land from. We handle the airspace checks, flight restriction zone checks and any landowner permissions before the day of the shoot, so there is nothing for you to arrange.</div></div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-q" type="button" aria-expanded="false">How will I receive the drone photographs?<span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">Images arrive edited and colour corrected, delivered digitally as high-resolution files you can use straight away in listings, reports, brochures and planning documents. If you are working to a deadline, tell us when you need them and we will agree a turnaround before the shoot.</div></div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-q" type="button" aria-expanded="false">Can you fly a drone in bad weather?<span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">Drones cannot fly safely in heavy rain or high winds, so we monitor the forecast and will move a booking if conditions are unsuitable. Light overcast conditions are often ideal for property photography because they produce even lighting with no harsh shadows on the roof or facade.</div></div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-q" type="button" aria-expanded="false">Do you carry out drone roof surveys for homeowners?<span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">Yes. A drone roof survey is a safe, non-invasive alternative to scaffolding or ladders. We photograph tiles, slates, flat roofs, chimneys, flashings, ridge tiles, guttering, fascias and soffits at high resolution, so you or your roofer can identify problems without anyone leaving the ground.</div></div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-q" type="button" aria-expanded="false">Which areas of West Yorkshire do you cover?<span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">We are based in Huddersfield and regularly cover Leeds, Halifax, Bradford, Wakefield, Dewsbury, Brighouse, Mirfield, Holmfirth, Batley, Cleckheaton and Barnsley. We also travel further across Yorkshire for larger commercial and development work.</div></div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-q" type="button" aria-expanded="false">Are you insured for drone photography work?<span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
